values ('a3b4c5d6-7e8f-4a78-9b88-9c0d1e2f3a08', 'introduction-to-hispanic-literature', 'Introduction to Hispanic Literature', 'This course introduces students to the formal study of Hispanic literature across Spain, Latin America, the Caribbean, and U.S. Latinx contexts. Students learn to read poetry, narrative, drama, essay, chronicle, testimony, and hybrid forms in Spanish while connecting close textual analysis to historical period, genre, canon formation, identity, and critical method. The course is designed as a bridge between advanced language work and upper-division seminars. Its main goal is to help students write precise, evidence-based literary arguments in Spanish while developing the vocabulary and intellectual habits needed for serious work in Hispanic literary studies.');

